meta {
  name: HCP fleet capacity (latest per cluster)
  type: http
  seq: 240
}

get {
  url: {{baseURL}}/recommendations/openshift/hcp/fleet-capacity
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  W4 fleet-capacity advisory (ros-ocp-backend #392; requires the hcp plugin).

  Returns the latest native published-sizing snapshot per management
  cluster authorized for the caller. Without a cluster filter: exactly one
  row per cluster (the card-list discovery surface). Narrow to one
  cluster with filter[cluster_uuid] (filter[cluster] and the bare
  cluster_uuid query param resolve identically).

  Each row carries the five scenarios (request, low_qps, average_qps,
  medium_qps, high_qps) with serve-time headroom: null when occupancy,
  worker placement, or average QPS is unknown, and withheld (null) when
  node pressure is affirmed — never derived client-side. An empty
  limiting_resource means the scenario has no estimate (render "not
  available", not 0). mce_references are the optional same-scenario MCE
  gauges: null = absent, never zero.

  warnings: stale (age over 2x the row's own max cadence),
  below_version_floor (known ocp_version under 4.17 — data still
  served), pressured, pressure_unknown, mce_may_be_stale (MCE gauges
  frozen across the freshness window while native inputs moved),
  shared_infrastructure (compact topology — control planes share the
  worker infrastructure; estimates may overstate dedicated capacity).

  Unknown or unauthorized clusters are non-disclosing: HTTP 200 with
  empty data, never 403/404.
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}
